    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: c0b9ac6c91fac2ba1d9fcabe20cc6735f3d48103 -->\nQuick read-only review (no build; author's build/tests/clippy taken as reported): clean.\n\n1. HolderHit is { at: usize, part: bool, short_mm: f64 } - a single move index, so the single-move arm is right (not Crossing, not unlocated).\n2. moves_named is exhaustive over all 11 variants: Crossing (pair arm), Gouge, ShankHit, SweepHit, RapidInStock, HolderHit (added), FixtureHit, NonFinite, Envelope, Scallop (single arm), RestUnjudged (the [None, None] arm per the test).\n3. The new assertion moves_named(HolderHit { at: 11, .. }) == [Some(11), None] is correct.\n4. Other Warning matches already carry HolderHit: mcp/job.rs:179, ui operations.rs:247 and :255. No other gap found.\n\nVerdict: merge-ready.\n",
